# fs-syscall-specs lane SH-TO-URUN, STAGES 1-2: the shell's program proof
# on the urun engine.  UCodeShK.v is a SECOND code catalog over the SAME
# dump as UCodeSh.v -- generated at [--prog shk] (tools/ucode_shk.txt) so
# the first-generation sh proofs (UProofSh*.v, still on-build over WpUmode*
# and UmodeIo's io-protocol) keep [sh_text_sub] / [ui_sh_*] / [sh_code]
# while the port gets [shk_text_sub] / [uis_shk_*] / [shk_code] over the
# same ShInstrs.sh_bytes.  It covers 192 instructions in 10 functions:
# start, main, getcmd, memset, gets and the open/close/exit/write/read
# stubs.  IT IS NO LONGER THE LANE'S COMPILE-TIME BUDGET.  A catalog used
# to cost ~22 s fixed plus ~1.9 s PER INSTRUCTION (192 instr = 320 s), and
# that is why this note used to say the parser's ~500 more belonged in a
# SECOND catalog file; the whole of it was ONE inline [ltac:] in [uis_run]
# (see the tactic's own comment, and optimization.md's "unshelve hoist").
# Hoisted, this file is 10.6 s and an instruction costs ~0.03 s, so a
# 700-instruction catalog would be well under a minute -- split it for
# readability if you like, but not for the build.
#   UkRunBr.v is the ONE branch leaf UkRunLeaf.v does not have and should
# ([wp_uk_btype0], the base branch against x0, whose value is not readable
# off the register file) -- a six-line re-thread of an existing UkBranch
# leaf.  RELOCATION ASK: it belongs beside [wp_uk_btype] in UkRunLeaf.v.
# The file's other leaf, [wp_uk_btype_later], is GONE from here: init's
# loops needed the same rule and it now lives in UkRunLeaf.v, which is
# where both always belonged.
#   UkSh.v is the walk: the quiet-row stub shape once ([wp_ksh_qstub],
# instantiated at open, close and write), exit, start, main's prologue, the
# console preamble (an iLoeb whose invariant is EMPTY -- its branches are
# case split on the abstract [uv_btaken] boolean, so the walk never learns
# what fd the kernel returned), and the COMMAND LOOP: getcmd -> write +
# memset + gets -> read, the leading-blank scan, and a second iLoeb whose
# invariant is the BUFFER plus five register constants.  The scan
# terminates on the NUL gets plants, which is the one place a fact about
# memory decides control flow.  ONE Hypothesis, [ush_read_leaf]: the
# general window ecall leaf, which UkRunSys.v does not have yet; it is
# spelled at [wp_uk_ecall_wait_null]'s idiom and every lemma that depends
# on it says so and carries it as an explicit argument.  memset and the
# scan do not.  The walk stops at 0x97a, taken as [ush_rest] -- an abstract
# continuation that takes the LOOP HEAD as its own premise, because the
# rest of main's body falls back into it.  Audit = the standing three,
# zero Admitted.
#   STAGE 5 grows the catalog to 326 instructions in 18 functions (runcmd,
# fork1 and the fork/exec/pipe/wait/dup/chdir stubs join it) and adds
# UkShRun.v, the COMMAND TREE walk: runcmd's prologue and its 0x1398 jump
# table, the five arms (EXEC, REDIR, PIPE, LIST, BACK) and fork1.  The
# recursion is ORDINARY STRUCTURAL INDUCTION on a finite tree -- the node
# predicate [ush_cmd] is a premise, not a parse, and stage 4 is what builds
# one -- with the stack budget [6 * ush_ht c] words, one 48-byte frame per
# level.  [ush_cmd] is PERSISTENT (every byte DfracDiscarded), which is
# what lets it cross a fork as a [UkFork.Forkable] payload; the three
# forking arms carry it, the jump table and (PIPE) the two fd words over.
# ONE Hypothesis, [ush_diag_leaf]: the diagnostic subtree -- panic and the
# two fprintf-and-die tails -- at its three entry pcs; UkShDiag.v below
# DISCHARGES it.  FOUR lane leaves, all RELOCATION ASKS:
# [wp_uk_cldq]/[wp_uk_clwq]/
# [wp_uk_lwuq] are UkRunMem's compressed loads and lwu at a DFRAC (their
# proofs already are), and [wp_uk_clw_text] is a real gap -- a four-byte
# load out of the TEXT half, which the jump table needs and which
# [wp_uk_lbu_text] only does one byte wide.  Audit = the standing three,
# zero Admitted, zero new Axiom.
#   THE DIAGNOSTIC SUBTREE (ask 7) is UkShDiag.v: panic (0x4a, 11
# instructions) on top of fprintf (0x10aa, 17), vprintf (0xdea, 250) and
# putc (0xd2e, 12), and it discharges [ush_diag_leaf] -- so
# [wp_kshr_runcmd_final] and [wp_kshr_fork1_final] are UNCONDITIONAL and
# the runcmd cone has no Hypothesis left.  IT IS UPSTREAM'S WALK AT SH'S
# ADDRESSES: sh and cat contain the same ulib printf, byte for byte, with
# sh's copies exactly 0x8da above cat's, so UkCatLit/UkCatPutc/
# UkCatVprintf/UkCatVprintfS/UkCatFprintf port as an address shift.  The
# one real generalisation is [shd_str]/[wp_shd_lbu], which abstract the
# '%s' argument over WHICH HALF of the heap holds it -- cat's is a heap
# string, sh's panic prints a .rodata literal -- so the '%s' arm is proved
# once for both instead of twice.  Audit = the standing three.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# SH'S COMMAND-TREE RUNNER IS ON-BUILD, AT THE SCOPE ITS RESOURCES REACH.
#
# UkShRun.v walks [runcmd] and [fork1] for a tree that is [ush_simple] --
# no REDIRECT and no PIPE node.  Those two arms are the two that MOVE THE
# DESCRIPTOR TABLE (REDIR is close-then-open, each half of a PIPE is
# close/dup/close/close), a descriptor move is spent against the program-
# side LEDGER ([UserFd.ustd] / [UkSh.ush_std]), and the walk carries the
# ledger only to FRAME it -- so the two arms are REFUTED from the premise
# rather than assumed away: [ush_cmd] pins the node's type word, so the
# jump table's rows 2 and 3 are as dead as its DEFAULT row.  It is the
# scope stage 4 already hands over (a line with no symbol byte parses to a
# single EXEC node), and the fd-row port is what takes the premise off.
# The deleted walks are recoverable: `git show 60a91c01b:iris/UkShRun.v`.
#
# THE ONE THING THE ENGINE OWES IT: a FOUR-BYTE LOAD OUT OF THE TEXT HALF.
# runcmd's jump table at 0x1398 and nulterminate's at 0x13b0 are .rodata,
# which shares the executable segment's pages, so the heap files them
# under the TEXT gname; [UkLoad.uk_load_ok] demands a WRITABLE target page
# (text bytes are stamped and outside the walker's map --
# claude-notes/projects/icache.md) and the tier's one text reader,
# [UkRunMem.wp_uk_lbu_text], is width-1 all the way down
# (WpUmodeTextLoad.v).  So UkShRun.v and UkShParse.v each carry the SAME
# statement as a named Hypothesis ([wp_uk_clw_text] / [ushp_clw_text_ok])
# and one engine leaf discharges both.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
